{
	"name": "Raise Hell",
	"type": "feature",
	"img": "icons/magic/fire/flame-burning-building.webp",
	"system": {
		"description": "<p>At 17th level, your reputation has long garnered you the wrong kind of attention, but with a ruckus at the right time you can leverage it in your favor. While in a town or city, you may spend your action making an Intimidation check against a DC of 12. On a success, you draw the guards down on your position. Roll a [[/r 1d6]] on initiative count 0. On a 6, four @UUID[Compendium.a5e.a5e-monsters.Actor.ef7tpqwh6mbh1yat]{Guard Squads} lead by a @UUID[Compendium.a5e.a5e-monsters.Actor.05xw3umyhise1ptt]{Champion Warrior} arrive and seek to pacify the situation by arresting everyone present. While the squads each attack your enemies first, the Champion Warrior seeks to engage the Sentinel directly, engaging other hostiles only if they cannot reach you or are attacked.</p>",
